00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:36,000
irregular frames

266
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:38,000
may also be selected.

267
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:40,000
Double-click to start in the blank area.

268
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:42,000
Then left-click to

269
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:44,000
establish the top of the irregular selection frame.

270
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:46,000
Finally,

271
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:48,000
go back to the starting point

272
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:50,000
and select the content of the frame together.

273
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:52,000
You can also

274
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:54,000
use the Ctrl key

275
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:56,000
to select the entire frame.

276
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:00,000
Press the shortcut key Y

277
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:02,000
to open the canvas.

278
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:04,000
Select a female model.

279
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:06,000
On the model,

280
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:08,000
right-click to increase to the work area.

281
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:12,000
Note that in the pop-up window,

282
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:14,000
select the option

283
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:16,000
to open the size and position in the costume.

284
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:18,000
Then click to confirm

285
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:20,000
and close the canvas.

286
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:22,000
Now,

287
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:24,000
the position of the 3D costume and the model

288
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:26,000
does not match.

289
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:28,000
Let's use the move tool

290
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:30,000
to move the 3D costume to the model.

291
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:32,000
In the 3D window,

292
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,000
still use the select move tool

293
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:36,000
to select the 3D costume.

294
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,000
Here is a little trick.

295
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:40,000
We can double-click

296
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:42,000
on the plate

297
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:44,000
to select all the plates

298
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:46,000
that have a sewing relationship.

299
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:48,000
Then this whole chain group

300
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:50,000
and then in any position of the costume,

301
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:52,000
left-click to drag

302
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:54,000
to move the costume.

303
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:56,000
Because the space movement is three-dimensional,

304
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:58,000
the mouse input

305
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:00,000
is based on the two-dimensional plane,

306
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:02,000
so this kind of operation

307
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:04,000
will cause the movement of the costume

308
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:06,000
to not meet the expected,

309
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:08,000
so it is not easy to control.

310
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:10,000
Therefore, it is recommended that

311
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:12,000
everyone use the positioning ball

312
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:14,000
to make more accurate movements.

313
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:16,000
When we select the 3D costume,

314
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:18,000
left-click on any position on the costume,

315
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,000
there will be a 3-line straight axis,

316
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,000
three arcs

317
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:24,000
and a square between the straight lines

318
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:26,000
to form the positioning ball tool.

319
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:28,000
The straight axis is used to control the parallel,

320
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:30,000
the arc controls the rotation,

321
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:32,000
and the square controls the parallel

322
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:34,000
in the plane.

323
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:36,000
There are three types of positioning balls

324
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:38,000
in the software,

325
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:40,000
respectively,

326
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:42,000
screen coordinates,

327
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:44,000
world coordinates

328
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:46,000
and horizontal coordinates.

329
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:48,000
What we are using now

330
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:50,000
is the screen coordinates.

331
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:52,000
The axis of the screen coordinate positioning ball

332
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:54,000
depends on your perspective.

333
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:56,000
When looking to try to change,

334
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:58,000
the axis of the positioning ball

335
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,000
will rotate with the camera.

336
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:02,000
For example, if you rotate the perspective,

337
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:04,000
you can find that the red axis

338
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:06,000
is always the left and right direction

339
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:08,000
of your current perspective.

340
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:10,000
Find the coordinates

341
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:12,000
on the right-click of the 3D blank area

342
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:14,000
and switch to the world coordinates.

343
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:16,000
The world coordinates

344
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:18,000
and the appearance of the screen coordinates

345
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:20,000
are slightly different.

346
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:22,000
It is made up of three two-way arrows,

347
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:24,000
three complete arcs

348
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:26,000
and three square surfaces.

349
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:28,000
The world coordinates positioning ball

350
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:30,000
is the basic axis of three-dimensional space.

351
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:32,000
As the axis of the positioning ball,

352
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:34,000
it has nothing to do with the screen and the object.

353
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:36,000
For example, if you rotate the perspective,

354
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:38,000
you can see that the red axis

355
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:40,000
is always pointing

356
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:42,000
to the left and right direction of the model,

357
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:44,000
which is the x-axis direction of 3D space.

358
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,000
When using the world coordinates,

359
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:50,000
when the arc and the straight line overlap,

360
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:52,000
pay attention to the need

361
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:54,000
to rotate the perspective slightly

362
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:56,000
to prevent the line overlap

363
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:58,000
from affecting the choice.

364
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:02,000
The horizontal coordinates

365
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:04,000
and the positioning ball

366
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:06,000
follow the object.

367
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:08,000
The axis of the positioning ball

368
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:10,000
appears in the orientation direction itself.

369
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:12,000
It is mainly used to adjust the virtual model joints

370
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:14,000
and to use it when designing movements.

371
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:16,000
Next, we use the positioning ball

372
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:18,000
to put the costume on the model.

373
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:20,000
You can try it.

374
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:22,000
Choose the positioning ball type

375
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:24,000
that you are used to.

376
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:26,000
Here we use the screen coordinates

377
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:28,000
for demonstration.

378
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:30,000
First, press the shortcut 2

379
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:32,000
to the front of the model.

380
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:34,000
Move the costume

381
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:36,000
to the front of the virtual model.

382
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:40,000
Then press the shortcut 4 or 6

383
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:42,000
to the side of the model.

384
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:44,000
Then press the shortcut 4 or 6

385
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:46,000
to the side of the model.

386
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:48,000
Move the costume to the model.

387
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:50,000
This ensures that the costume

388
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:52,000
is worn on the model

389
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:54,000
in the direction of the policy.

390
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:56,000
After wearing it,

391
00:17:56,000 --> 00:17:58,000
rotate the angle to confirm

392
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:00,000
whether it is placed correctly.

393
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:02,000
Pay attention to the moving process.

394
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:04,000
You need to keep the whole costume

395
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:06,000
selected together,

396
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:08,000
then move it,

397
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:10,000
otherwise only one version will appear.

398
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:12,000
The whole costume

399
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,000
does not follow the movement.

400
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:16,000
In the window,

401
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:18,000
you can see that

402
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:20,000
when moving the 3D costume,

403
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:22,000
the 2D panel will not be misplaced.

404
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:24,000
Similarly,

405
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:26,000
use the adjustment panel tool

406
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:28,000
in the 2D window

407
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:30,000
to drag the moving panel.

408
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:32,000
The position of the 3D costume

409
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:34,000
will not be affected.

410
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:36,000
After the costume and model are matched,

411
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:38,000
we need to start the simulation.

412
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:40,000
Simulate the real fabric spiral

413
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:42,000
so that the costume is worn on the model.

414
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:44,000
Use the first tool in the upper left corner

415
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,000
to start the simulation.

416
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,000
When starting the simulation,

417
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:50,000
the 3D window will simulate

418
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:52,000
the real weight effect.

419
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:54,000
The panel will also show

420
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:56,000
the real soft fabric properties.

421
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:58,000
At this time,

422
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:00,000
the mouse will become a small grip

423
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:02,000
to adjust the shape of the costume.

424
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:04,000
You can left-click to drag the dress

425
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:06,000
to adjust the shape.

426
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:08,000
The shortcut key for simulation

427
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:10,000
is the control key.

428
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:12,000
Left-click to press the simulation tool.

429
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:14,000
Here are three different

430
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:16,000
simulation modes

431
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:18,000
to adapt to different work stages.

432
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:20,000
Normal speed default simulation mode

433
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:22,000
This is the most common mode.

434
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:24,000
Use it when making costumes.

435
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:26,000
Try the fabric properties

436
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:28,000
to calculate the simulation mode.

437
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:30,000
This mode will calculate

438
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:32,000
the physical properties

439
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:34,000
of the simulated fabric more accurately.

440
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:36,000
If you need to observe

441
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:38,000
the real fabric spiral

442
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:40,000
or the strength of the fabric,

443
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:42,000
it is recommended to switch to this option.

444
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:44,000
In contrast,

445
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:46,000
the calculation of this mode

446
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:48,000
is relatively advanced.

447
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:50,000
Animation completion simulation mode

448
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:52,000
Use it when making animation.

449
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:54,000
In addition,

450
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:56,000
at the bottom of the menu,

451
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:58,000
you can also choose

452
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:00,000
to calculate the engine as CPU or GPU.

453
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:02,000
GPU simulation can maintain

454
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:04,000
the same simulation accuracy

455
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:06,000
than the speed of CPU simulation.

456
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:08,000
Therefore,

457
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,000
it is more recommended to use the GPU simulation mode.

458
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:12,000
Switch to GPU simulation.

459
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:14,000
You can see that

460
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:16,000
the simulation icon will

461
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:18,000
turn from the 10-star arrow

462
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:20,000
to the down-to-earth air star arrow.

463
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:22,000
Press the control grid button to start the simulation.

464
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:24,000
The icon will turn blue.

465
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:26,000
Press the control grid button

466
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:28,000
to stop the simulation

467
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:30,000
and it will turn gray.

468
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:32,000
This is convenient for us to judge

469
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:34,000
the current simulation mode

470
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:36,000
and the calculation engine.

471
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:38,000
Finally,

472
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:56,000
let's take a look at the

473
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:58,000
simulation mode.

474
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:00,000
This is the simulation mode

475
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:02,000
of the GPU simulation mode.

476
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:04,000
This is the simulation mode

477
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:06,000
of the GPU simulation mode

478
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:08,000
for GPU simulation.

479
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:10,000
In this simulation mode,

480
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:12,000
the resulting resolution

481
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:15,119
level may be more 0.6ARE

482
00:21:15,119 --> 00:21:19,140
or

483
00:21:19,140 --> 00:21:21,140
2500 px.

484
00:21:21,140 --> 00:21:22,799
The simulation mode

485
00:21:22,799 --> 00:21:24,799
betrayed the simulation mode.

486
00:21:24,799 --> 00:21:26,660
If the simulation mode

487
00:21:26,660 --> 00:21:28,660
is set to 0,

488
00:21:28,660 --> 00:21:29,859
the simulation modul

489
00:21:29,859 --> 00:21:30,839
can be read as 0.6

490
00:21:30,839 --> 00:21:32,000
or 300 px.

491
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:32,759
However,

492
00:21:32,759 --> 00:21:34,400
when switching spin

493
00:21:34,400 --> 00:21:35,799
the simulation mode

494
00:21:35,799 --> 00:21:38,299
You can hide the inner line and the base line.

495
00:21:41,559 --> 00:21:45,500
In addition, you can see the blue icon in the vertical menu bar.

496
00:21:46,099 --> 00:21:49,480
Clothing

497
00:21:49,480 --> 00:21:51,559
Now 3D clothing is displayed on the surface of the fabric.

498
00:21:51,859 --> 00:21:57,059
The surface of the 3D clothing shows that the fabric is real fabric, and the reverse shows that it is gray.

499
00:21:57,700 --> 00:22:03,039
It can be distinguished by the opposite of the fabric, and the thickness of the fabric in this state is not displayed.

500
00:22:03,039 --> 00:22:09,599
After the general completion of the clothing, we can render the clothing type.

501
00:22:09,599 --> 00:22:17,039
Switch to the surface of the dense fabric, the 3D clothing will show the real thickness of the fabric and the exact back fabric.

502
00:22:19,539 --> 00:22:23,639
Finally, we can save the finished clothing file.

503
00:22:24,480 --> 00:22:30,480
Find the left corner file, save the project file, and set the file name in the pop-up window.

504
00:22:32,339 --> 00:22:32,879
At the same time,

505
00:22:32,880 --> 00:22:40,480
note that the file format we save is ZPRJ, which is the most commonly used project file format in CLO.

506
00:22:40,480 --> 00:22:48,780
The file will contain 3D clothing, virtual models, rendering attribute settings, animation information, and other information such as color.

507
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:56,040
In addition, the common format in CLO also contains ZPAC clothing files,

508
00:22:57,380 --> 00:23:01,280
AVT virtual model files, ZFAB fabric files,

509
00:23:01,279 --> 00:23:04,119
BTN button buttons, and so on.

